---
// Five nested engineering paradigms: each wider layer contains the one before it.
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 320"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d-ep-title d-ep-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d-ep-title">Nested engineering paradigms</title>
	<desc id="d-ep-desc">
		Five nested layers, from outermost to innermost: graph engineering, an explicit execution graph; loop engineering,
		sustained runs; harness engineering, the system around the model; context engineering, everything the model sees;
		and prompt engineering. Each layer contains the previous one.
	</desc>

	<g class="dg-container dg-neutral">
		<rect x="12" y="12" width="696" height="296" rx="14"></rect>
		<text x="28" y="40" font-weight="700">Graph engineering: explicit execution graph</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-container dg-neutral">
		<rect x="36" y="52" width="648" height="236" rx="12"></rect>
		<text x="52" y="80" font-weight="700">Loop engineering: sustained runs</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-container dg-harness">
		<rect x="60" y="92" width="600" height="176" rx="12"></rect>
		<text x="76" y="120" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">Harness engineering: the system around the model</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-container dg-context">
		<rect x="84" y="132" width="552" height="116" rx="12"></rect>
		<text x="100" y="160" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">Context engineering: everything the model sees</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-container dg-model">
		<rect x="108" y="172" width="504" height="56" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="124" y="206" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">Prompt engineering</text>
	</g>
</svg>
